1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,043
This is the Corsair Queen after today.

2
00:00:03,493 --> 00:00:06,537
The crew is told she is here.

3
00:00:06,987 --> 00:00:10,465
They have ten minutes to sink her flagship.

4
00:00:10,915 --> 00:00:14,393
There is a bonus for her second ship.

5
00:00:14,843 --> 00:00:19,626
And ninety seconds in, a third ship she was holding back.

6
00:00:20,076 --> 00:00:23,554
Three of those are lines you already know.

7
00:00:24,004 --> 00:00:26,178
The last is one card.

8
00:00:27,378 --> 00:00:29,117
Same as last time.

9
00:00:29,567 --> 00:00:33,915
Low one hundred percent, so she arrives four seconds in.

10
00:00:34,365 --> 00:00:38,278
We put the real number back at the end.

11
00:00:39,478 --> 00:00:44,261
Before we change her story, read the Siege's own. Four quests.

12
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:50,363
Repel the Siege is the top: finish it and the game is won.

13
00:00:50,813 --> 00:00:56,900
Break the Siege is required, and it is done when every raider is gone.

14
00:00:57,350 --> 00:01:00,828
The other two are the ways to lose.

15
00:01:01,278 --> 00:01:03,452
Now look at your objective.

16
00:01:03,902 --> 00:01:05,207
Parent, siege mission.

17
00:01:05,657 --> 00:01:08,700
That line hangs it on this tree.

18
00:01:09,150 --> 00:01:14,802
Required true means one more thing the crew must finish before they win.

19
00:01:15,252 --> 00:01:18,296
Leave Required off, and it is extra.

20
00:01:19,496 --> 00:01:23,409
Sink the Morrigan has never meant sink the Morrigan.

21
00:01:23,859 --> 00:01:25,598
It meant destroy everything.

22
00:01:26,048 --> 00:01:29,961
One line fixes it: done when, destroy one morrigan.

23
00:01:30,411 --> 00:01:32,585
Morrigan here is a role.

24
00:01:33,035 --> 00:01:38,687
Every named ship gets its own name, in small letters, as a role.

25
00:01:39,137 --> 00:01:43,920
And I add an objective line, the sentence the crew reads.

26
00:01:44,370 --> 00:01:50,891
Now the objective is done when she is, and the reward is paid right then.

27
00:01:51,341 --> 00:01:56,993
The game is not over yet: Break the Siege still wants every raider.

28
00:01:58,193 --> 00:01:59,498
A second objective.

29
00:01:59,948 --> 00:02:02,122
Two hashes, like the first.

30
00:02:02,572 --> 00:02:05,180
Destroy one badb, three hundred credits.

31
00:02:05,630 --> 00:02:07,370
And no Required line.

32
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:14,341
So it is a bonus: pay if they do it, win if they do not.

33
00:02:15,541 --> 00:02:16,846
Now a clock.

34
00:02:17,296 --> 00:02:19,904
Three lines, and they go together.

35
00:02:20,354 --> 00:02:24,267
Fails when, thirty seconds: a test number. Fatal true.

36
00:02:24,717 --> 00:02:28,630
And Lose, with the sentence the crew will read.

37
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:32,124
I start the game and do nothing.

38
00:02:32,574 --> 00:02:36,052
Thirty seconds after she arrives... there. My sentence.

39
00:02:36,502 --> 00:02:39,111
Now the real number, ten minutes.

40
00:02:39,561 --> 00:02:40,865
One more thing.

41
00:02:41,315 --> 00:02:44,359
Nobody warns the crew about this clock.

42
00:02:44,809 --> 00:02:51,765
So I say it where they will read it: in the objective, and in the description.

43
00:02:52,965 --> 00:02:56,009
One more line an objective can have.

44
00:02:56,459 --> 00:02:58,198
Win, and a sentence.

45
00:02:58,648 --> 00:03:04,300
Now the game is won the moment she sinks, whatever else is flying.

46
00:03:04,750 --> 00:03:08,228
For some bosses that is the right ending.

47
00:03:08,678 --> 00:03:12,591
Not for this one, because of what is coming.

48
00:03:13,041 --> 00:03:15,650
So I take it out again.

49
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:21,752
Required, Win, and the three lines for losing: those are your three endings.

50
00:03:22,952 --> 00:03:25,561
Some things no line can say.

51
00:03:26,011 --> 00:03:34,707
For those a boss has a hook: a named block of script that the Siege runs once, when she arrives.

52
00:03:35,157 --> 00:03:37,330
One comes with the game.

53
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:39,085
Hook, biomech infestation.

54
00:03:39,535 --> 00:03:41,274
And there they are.

55
00:03:41,724 --> 00:03:43,463
I wrote no script.

56
00:03:43,913 --> 00:03:46,522
But BioMechs are not her story.

57
00:03:47,722 --> 00:03:53,809
Her own hook is a label, and a label lives in a mast file.

58
00:03:54,259 --> 00:03:56,433
Here is the awkward part.

59
00:03:56,883 --> 00:04:02,100
Her boss file is in common data, where updates never touch it.

60
00:04:02,550 --> 00:04:04,724
A hook cannot go there.

61
00:04:05,174 --> 00:04:07,783
It has to be inside LegendaryMissions.

62
00:04:08,233 --> 00:04:15,624
So I make a folder of my own in there, corsair queen, and one file in it.

63
00:04:16,074 --> 00:04:20,857
The name is exact: two underscores, init, two underscores, dot mast.

64
00:04:21,307 --> 00:04:24,785
The game reads every file with that name.

65
00:04:25,985 --> 00:04:28,159
Now the card does more.

66
00:04:28,609 --> 00:04:30,783
Wait: you know this one.

67
00:04:31,233 --> 00:04:32,972
Ten seconds for testing.

68
00:04:33,422 --> 00:04:37,335
Then a guard: if the game is over, stop.

69
00:04:37,785 --> 00:04:39,524
Then the ship line.

70
00:04:39,974 --> 00:04:43,452
It is long, and it is one line.

71
00:04:43,902 --> 00:04:52,598
You change four things: where, her name, her ship key, and her role, which is her name in small letters.

72
00:04:53,048 --> 00:04:57,830
Last, finish a step: your other card, with a signal name.

73
00:04:59,030 --> 00:05:00,770
Lint, clean. Compile, nothing.

74
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:06,437
Four seconds: she is here, and so is the sentence. Three objectives.

75
00:05:06,887 --> 00:05:10,365
Ten seconds... the Nemain, and a fourth objective.

76
00:05:10,815 --> 00:05:12,989
Now the mistake nothing catches.

77
00:05:13,439 --> 00:05:16,483
One letter wrong in the Hook line.

78
00:05:16,933 --> 00:05:18,237
Lint is happy.

79
00:05:18,687 --> 00:05:19,991
Compile is happy.

80
00:05:20,441 --> 00:05:23,485
And the game stops when she arrives.

81
00:05:23,935 --> 00:05:27,413
So check that word by eye, every time.

82
00:05:28,613 --> 00:05:29,917
Testing is over.

83
00:05:30,367 --> 00:05:35,150
Forty percent, ninety seconds, and the note brought up to date.

84
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:38,209
One last thing, and it matters.

85
00:05:38,659 --> 00:05:41,702
Her boss file is safe from updates.

86
00:05:42,152 --> 00:05:48,239
Her hook is not: it is inside LegendaryMissions, and an update replaces that folder.

87
00:05:48,689 --> 00:05:54,776
Then she is still in the list, and the game stops when she arrives.

88
00:05:55,226 --> 00:06:01,748
So keep a copy of this folder outside, and put it back after every update.

89
00:06:02,948 --> 00:06:04,687
Your own boss now.

90
00:06:05,137 --> 00:06:14,267
An objective that means what it says, a bonus, a clock, an ending you chose, and one sentence when it arrives.

91
00:06:14,717 --> 00:06:17,326
Next time she gets a voice.
